      {
        "question_text": "Use the area model for $24\\times37$.\n(a) Find the four part-products.\n(b) Find the total.\n[tikz]\\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]\n\\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,3);\n\\draw (2.5,0)--(2.5,3);\n\\draw (0,1.5)--(5,1.5);\n\\node[above] at (1.25,3) {$20$};\n\\node[above] at (3.75,3) {$4$};\n\\node[left] at (0,2.25) {$30$};\n\\node[left] at (0,0.75) {$7$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "(a) Multiply each row label by each column label.\n[tikz]\\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]\n\\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,3);\n\\draw (2.5,0)--(2.5,3);\n\\draw (0,1.5)--(5,1.5);\n\\node[above] at (1.25,3) {$20$};\n\\node[above] at (3.75,3) {$4$};\n\\node[left] at (0,2.25) {$30$};\n\\node[left] at (0,0.75) {$7$};\n\\node at (1.25,2.25) {$600$};\n\\node at (3.75,2.25) {$120$};\n\\node at (1.25,0.75) {$140$};\n\\node at (3.75,0.75) {$28$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]\n$\\begin{aligned}20\\times30&=600 & 4\\times30&=120\\\\20\\times7&=140 & 4\\times7&=28\\end{aligned}$\n(b) Add all four part-products.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}24\\times37\\\\&=600+120+140+28\\\\&=888\\end{aligned}$"
      }
    ],
